## Bounded disposition and work assessment

Even strengthening the gate to diagnostics=nothing, both limits infinite, explicit
ordinary switch values and a fixed hardware scalar/backend would leave a separate
proof obligation for default arithmetic failures and scratch/cache initialization.
This is an unresolved requirement, not a demonstrated counterexample to that
stronger subset. No pre-existing immutable certificate establishes those facts.
A data-dependent eligibility scan/direct slack arithmetic would be a different
proposal. Finite input checks alone would not prove finite intermediate arithmetic.
Recreating the ordered operations to predict their outcome could spend the work
being removed; it must not be hidden inside a nominally constant-time predicate.
This step neither constructs such a predicate nor proves none could exist.

At most the proposed deletion targets ONE cold default reconstruction per cleanup
invocation: one checked FTRAN, one checked BTRAN, one pricing pass, plus validation,
mask/RHS initialization and state/coefficient traversals, O(m+n+nnz(A)) outside
backend solves. Constructor/factor ownership, restored refactor/reconstruction,
projection, ordinary steps and original certification remain. Active checked
checkpoint copies are additional and ineligible under the proposed ordinary scope.
No new initialization saving has been measured. S5-C only removes one eligible
O(m+n) restoration cost copy; bound copies remain required.

